# ── HARD PRIVACY GUARD — do not weaken ──────────────────────────────────────
# This app READS a personal book library at runtime. No book content, and no
# path to it, may ever be committed. These rules are belt-and-suspenders so an
# accidental `git add .` cannot leak the library. See README §Privacy.

# Every common book / document format, anywhere in the tree:
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw
*.azw3
*.djvu
*.cbz
*.cbr
*.fb2
*.txt          # books often arrive as .txt — code uses .py, so this is safe to block
*.md.book      # any exported book text

# Any local data / library / cache directory the app might create:
/data/
/library/
/books/
/cache/
/audio_cache/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg

# The real config (which contains the absolute path to your library) is local-only.
# Only config.example.toml is committed.
config.toml
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
